<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Fact check: Three viral Iran war posts debunked</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:112341debdccffb0ebcba0f29623de20729ec3b690ad6ef4cdf5dc53366feb33</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T15:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-three-viral-iran-war-posts-debunked/a-79867353--97b07015723a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-three-viral-iran-war-posts-debunked/a-79867353?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In the wake of the new US attack on Iran, social media is awash with dramatic images and claims about the fighting. DW Fact Check found AI-generated and recycled videos, as well as misleading posts from dubious accounts.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Protests and reforms: France's rising debt costs threaten stability</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c259f5c523433eb39f8531fe5703f947192493678b76d544b79d7959b854583</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/protests-and-reforms-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654--ed74af6123ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/protests-and-reforms-france-s-rising-debt-costs-threaten-stability/a-79865654?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France plans to spend an extra €4 billion on education amid nationwide protests. But with public debt mounting and interest costs climbing, how much fiscal room does the government have?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Czech arms makers set sights on space defense in bid to sustain Ukraine-driven arms boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cda5df648ca9b59bc04e0328bd4cac931f25c08bfb6bfb2c2546b4abed021bb</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T14:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czech-arms-makers-set-sights-on-space-defense-in-bid-to-sustain-ukraine-driven-arms-boom/a-79876035--897a0df46a70.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czech-arms-makers-set-sights-on-space-defense-in-bid-to-sustain-ukraine-driven-arms-boom/a-79876035?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Czech arms makers have thrived on demand linked to the war in Ukraine. To sustain their growth, they need to look beyond ammunition and toward new technologies — and even space.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Zambia's civil service overhaul raises questions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fdb6637ad7152c95d919d3bac50124f8ddd96690f570061717c4c85733d4a08c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-civil-service-overhaul-raises-questions/a-79875892--d33c313a06f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zambia-s-civil-service-overhaul-raises-questions/a-79875892?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Government-backed retirements and institutional realignments are fueling debate in Zambia, with opposition politicians questioning transparency while officials defend the changes as necessary reforms.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the IIHF Women's Ice Hockey World Championship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5e0a14396bda894cf08fe82989d9c8e34651344e5fc80a9952475ccf515417b</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148--d773b0d8af6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As ice hockey's governing body continues to wrangle over how to respond to a CAS order to reinstate Russia to international play, the top women's tournament gets underway in Denmark. Without Russia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Global temperatures are set to exceed 1.5 degrees above pre-industrial levels in 2026, likely the second-warmest year on record</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:294c8e74cd65801e548bff56226523fe151dfbf8c1fecd3129b984223efe6aa0</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-temperatures-are-set-to-exceed-1-5-degrees-above-pre-industrial-levels-in-2026-likely-the-sec/a-79874098--d560bb827fee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-temperatures-are-set-to-exceed-1-5-degrees-above-pre-industrial-levels-in-2026-likely-the-second-warmest-year-on-record/a-79874098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate scientists say the world is set to breach the critical 1.5-degree Celsius threshold in 2026. This year is also on track to become the second-warmest on record.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>For people in Iran, a constant threat of war and dearth of information</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a2031687bd96dc30a97fbb0365e3502135be5aad506c142169ffefd2ae5b178</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:01:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/for-people-in-iran-a-constant-threat-of-war-and-dearth-of-information/a-79875438--15c623b3dc73.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/for-people-in-iran-a-constant-threat-of-war-and-dearth-of-information/a-79875438?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Most people in Iran have little idea of the course of the US-led war and peace talks on the global stage. With few sources of information, the population must navigate conflicting rumors and fears of a nuclear attack.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>New bomb threats target Irish media, more European flights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88b930a5fb53b8e81643cc139f2fba2c82e99029e800f25a080ff80f21e82fa0</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:00Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-bomb-threats-target-irish-media-more-european-flights/a-79875884--2150fa159109.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-bomb-threats-target-irish-media-more-european-flights/a-79875884?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Newsrooms have been evacuated across Ireland after another wave of bomb threats. Dublin is hosting a high-level EU meeting in several days.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tanzania: Opposition leader Tundu Lissu jailed for four years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0121f22d6bdf827a48c94c1cda62ea06ff8d201c569858048de43c6e5a24b34d</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tanzania-opposition-leader-tundu-lissu-jailed-for-four-years/a-79875248--8689ad1af62d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tanzania-opposition-leader-tundu-lissu-jailed-for-four-years/a-79875248?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu has been sentenced to four years in prison after being cleared of treason. Lissu condemned his conviction for incitement, which had not been among the charges he faced.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'No choice but to bear it': Delhi's unrelenting air pollution crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b9469ac109942a427969a4d1d18ea5450c70a57666d722fefc3973cc84e579d</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124--aa42da1e16d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite years of government interventions, emergency restrictions and public outrage, Delhi continues to battle dangerously polluted air every winter. Why isn't there a lasting solution to a predictable crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya cult leader Paul Mackenzie sentenced to 200 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11f319b7c98b64c77f9499004e8b7cea386e6190655233aaaafa612dfd15cd50</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-paul-mackenzie-sentenced-to-200-years/a-79875112--7a13b520397b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-paul-mackenzie-sentenced-to-200-years/a-79875112?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court in Kenya has sentenced Paul Mackenzie to 200 years in prison for the murders of 190 children and an adult. He told them to starve themselves to death as part of his apocalyptic religious cult.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Exercise and cancer: What "living longer" really means</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0182886fd1ed3a76017d8f613457ba21dbe7608e45c442928cf49f59bccc4a43</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/exercise-and-cancer-what-living-longer-really-means/a-79856133--580b8e4a11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/exercise-and-cancer-what-living-longer-really-means/a-79856133?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major trial found more colon cancer patients were alive eight years after treatment with long-term exercise coaching. But what does "living longer" mean, and who does it apply to?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Ex-minister arrested in a major fund manipulation scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7704540e5c8db40cb177ec50b6586cf12bf4488ee3779bfbf3754af353694fa2</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-ex-minister-arrested-in-a-major-fund-manipulation-scandal/a-79872732--6080246c24d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-ex-minister-arrested-in-a-major-fund-manipulation-scandal/a-79872732?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatma Betul Sayan Kaya, a former deputy chair of President Erdogan's party, was arrested in a major funds scandal. The opposition claims Sayan Kaya and her husband cashed in shares worth millions in the illegal scheme.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>French bus carrying school children crashes, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71bc5fdb7f3d387084c8f30a6076fd75217fbe594266801ece888dcfe1b7311c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-bus-carrying-school-children-crashes-killing-2/a-79873221--5ed9a6b7c1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-bus-carrying-school-children-crashes-killing-2/a-79873221?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bus reportedly veered off the road and crashed into a tree. French Transport Minister Philippe Tabarot was on his way to the scene.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European shares join a global sell-off as AI spending fears rattle Wall Street and Asian markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:708ac65d0fdba7828cbd1233a2c1c6289fa7f3a207e46c1765525a3d854f5fb6</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-shares-join-a-global-sell-off-as-ai-spending-fears-rattle-wall-street-and-asian-markets/a-79871504--c1f154c43d0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-shares-join-a-global-sell-off-as-ai-spending-fears-rattle-wall-street-and-asian-markets/a-79871504?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European shares have fallen after sharp losses in Asia and on Wall Street. Doubts over huge AI investments and fears of curbs following the Democrats' US midterm victory have rattled global markets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo sets off on 12-day South America tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9132ae8b6ccb61d3c90e28fa1ca5d61411559de0a8481278b1281620ecc911d</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-sets-off-on-12-day-south-america-tour/a-79872584--6d3b3fa5e428.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-sets-off-on-12-day-south-america-tour/a-79872584?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pontiff will hold meetings and celebrate Mass in Uruguay, Argentina and Peru, with the latter attracting particular interest. The trip will be the longest and farthest of his papacy so far.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia: Ex-leader Najib seeks to leave prison for house arrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2803bce0f32104cc4fddc6f44111919fe25a34b043f15bfb623ce97cb8c3a157</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/malaysia-ex-leader-najib-seeks-to-leave-prison-for-house-arrest/a-79872493--d3d9aa9ab49e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/malaysia-ex-leader-najib-seeks-to-leave-prison-for-house-arrest/a-79872493?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Convicted for embezzlement, former Prime Minister Najib Razak hopes to serve his prison term under house arrest after his party paid a fine. But the attorney general later said his transfer was on hold temporarily.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Trial of alleged 'Reichsbürger' group ringleaders begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:112ceccf4a6d05ccc98217b47cc04e9264e277ca20854584106bd1265a0f7f7c</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-of-alleged-reichsb_rger-group-ringleaders-begins/live-79872046--a2b502d3bfa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-trial-of-alleged-reichsbürger-group-ringleaders-begins/live-79872046?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Four members of the banned far-right "Kingdom of Germany" are on trial for belonging to a criminal organization. Meanwhile, a new study warns data centers could lead to water stress in Germany. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Umar Khalid, Sharjeel Imam go back to Supreme Court for bail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34d165741d7facf0472c47a31cb3da6fdc9511a60262eb767d2e5878f08d6756</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:02:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T07:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-umar-khalid-sharjeel-imam-go-back-to-supreme-court-for-bail/live-79872047--7c00fb66e611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-umar-khalid-sharjeel-imam-go-back-to-supreme-court-for-bail/live-79872047?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Umar Khalid and Sharjeel Imam have asked the Supreme Court for bail once more, having spent over six years in jail. Elsewhere, the top court has clarified when the 24-hour clock for producing an arrested person starts.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US judge temporarily blocks Trump's arch project after panel approval</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45ad0899d179bd998fdeaa0028e8d5cdcdf6b529d2f4762c4b4486d4ccb44261</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T06:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-judge-temporarily-blocks-trump-s-arch-project-after-panel-approval/a-79871690--3c90724774bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-judge-temporarily-blocks-trump-s-arch-project-after-panel-approval/a-79871690?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A judge ordered a two-week stop to construction on US President Trump's arch project in Washington. A federal panel had approved Trump's triumphal arch plans in an 8-4 vote.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ex-lawmaker jailed in Macau's first national security trial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd44c480510fe5c189c710d0949ca2a487f1201daca0659d89590a9e561e249e</id><updated>2026-11-06T16:00:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T04:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ex-lawmaker-jailed-in-macau-s-first-national-security-trial/a-79871673--02ef64bcc21e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ex-lawmaker-jailed-in-macau-s-first-national-security-trial/a-79871673?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pro-democracy former lawmaker Au Kam San was found guilty of "subversion against the political power of the State." He was handed a prison sentence of 12-and-a-half years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
